+title: Documentation
+description: Install mpvRx, choose a build, tune playback, connect media sources, and extend the player with Lua or JavaScript.
+---
+
+Practical guides for installing, configuring, and extending mpvRx. Start with a stable default setup, then add only the playback, library, and automation features you need.
+
+<CardGroup cols={2}>
+	<Card title="Install mpvRx" href="/docs/getting-started/installation" icon="download">
+		Choose a trusted release, variant, and CPU architecture.
+	</Card>
+	<Card title="Start playback" href="/docs/getting-started/first-playback" icon="play">
+		Establish a clean playback baseline before advanced tuning.
+	</Card>
+	<Card title="Tune the player" href="/docs/playback/controls-and-gestures" icon="sliders-horizontal">
+		Configure gestures, controls, video, audio, and subtitles.
+	</Card>
+	<Card title="Connect your library" href="/docs/library-and-streaming/local-and-network" icon="folder-network">
+		Browse local storage, SMB, FTP, SFTP, and WebDAV.
+	</Card>
+	<Card title="Script mpvRx" href="/docs/customization/scripting" icon="code-2">
+		Load Lua or JavaScript and call native mpvRx commands.
+	</Card>
+	<Card title="Fix a problem" href="/docs/reference/troubleshooting" icon="wrench">
+		Isolate playback, library, server, and configuration issues.
+	</Card>
+</CardGroup>
+
+## What mpvRx covers
+
+- Local video and music libraries
+- Network shares and direct URLs
+- Jellyfin and Navidrome/Subsonic servers
+- Torrent, HLS, MP4, and supported online sources
+- HDR pipelines, shaders, Anime4K, ambient effects, and filters
+- Dual subtitles, online search, styling, and speech-to-subtitle tools
+- Google Cast, picture-in-picture, background playback, and playlists
+- `mpv.conf`, `input.conf`, Lua, JavaScript, and custom player buttons
+
+:::note
+Device codecs, GPU drivers, server features, and remote media formats vary. The docs identify where behavior depends on the device or external service.
+:::
